WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.500
Let’s work that trap through, so you’ve done it once before the exam.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.625
Follow it on screen.

3
00:00:06.875 --> 00:00:09.825
You’re steering zero four five by compass.

4
00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:14.125
Your deviation card shows two degrees west on that heading.

5
00:00:14.375 --> 00:00:17.100
Variation is five degrees west.

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.775
You take a bearing on a lighthouse, and the compass reads one two zero.

7
00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:23.975
Which deviation?

8
00:00:24.225 --> 00:00:27.050
The one for zero four five, your heading.

9
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.825
Two west.

10
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:33.350
And we’re correcting, compass toward true, so west is subtracted.

11
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.625
One two zero minus two is one one eight, magnetic.

12
00:00:37.875 --> 00:00:40.400
Now variation, five west.

13
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.375
Subtract again.

14
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:46.150
One one eight minus five is one one three, true.

15
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.375
And what goes on the chart?

16
00:00:49.375 --> 00:00:51.125
One one three.

17
00:00:51.375 --> 00:00:53.925
Bearings are always plotted as true.

18
00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:56.050
That’s lesson nine.

19
00:00:56.300 --> 00:01:00.150
True, variation, magnetic, deviation, compass.

20
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:02.375
Correcting, add east.

21
00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:05.225
Deviation goes with your heading.

22
00:01:05.475 --> 00:01:07.700
Compass least, error east.

23
00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:11.800
Next time: headings, bearings and checking your compass.
